//? Title: Insertion Sort: Actual Shifts, Stable Identities and Existing Order
//? Subtitle: One executing kernel, exact inversion counts and the original seed-one experiment
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Put integer records into nondecreasing order while preserving the order of equal
keys. Insertion sort grows a sorted prefix by shifting only predecessors larger
than the held key. We start with three values, preserve the original seven-value
trace and shuffled experiment, and derive exact comparison and shift identities.
All observations come from the library's executing loop. The working vector is
sorted in place, but the public by-value call copies lvalue input; neither low
comparison counts nor this experiment establishes a universal runtime advantage.
)
\toc

> Start with one insertion

For [3,1,2], the first insertion holds key one, shifts three right and places
one at position zero. Its one key comparison succeeds; reaching the left
boundary ends the loop without an extra false key comparison. The next insertion
shifts three, then compares one with two and stops. These are actual boundaries,
not results reconstructed by sorting each input prefix again.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/insertion_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::insertion_sort_trace({3, 1, 2});
    std::print("| insertion | key | destination | comparisons | shifts | actual values |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &x : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", x.index, x.key,
                   x.destination, x.comparisons, x.shifts, x.values);
    std::print("Final values {}, identities {}, comparisons {}, shifts {}, placements {}.\n",
               t.run.values, t.run.identities, t.run.work.comparisons,
               t.run.work.shifts, t.run.work.placements);
    dm::algorithms::insertion_sort_step_diagram(t).save_svg(
        "build/insertion_tiny.svg");
}
```
