> Preserve the original evolving shuffle experiment

The next block preserves the original forty sizes 5,10,…,200, the single
evolving std::mt19937 seed-one stream and each std::shuffle invocation. One
shuffled input at each size is one observation, not an estimated average. The
shuffle mapping is toolchain-specific; the native profile retains its actual
inputs for checking. The sorted/reversed inputs are deterministic. On this
toolchain the final shuffled count is 10652, not the old cached 10466; the
extracted original count function and the shared kernel agree on every actual
generated input. All three costs now come from the same executing library kernel
rather than a copied instrumented implementation.

For a uniformly random permutation of distinct keys, each pair is inverted with
probability one-half, so E[I]=n(n−1)/4. Position i is a strict new minimum with
probability 1/(i+1), giving E[M]=Hₙ−1. Consequently,

$$
\mathbb{E}[C]=\frac{n(n-1)}4+n-H_n.
$$
\alttext(Uniform distinct permutations have expected comparison count n times n minus one over four, plus n minus the nth harmonic number.)

That is a distributional identity, not a guarantee for the single seed-one
permutation. No crossover against another sorting algorithm is measured here.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/insertion_profile.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto rows = dm::algorithms::insertion_sort_example_profile();
    std::vector<double> n, random, sorted, reversed;
    std::print("| n | sorted comparisons | shuffled comparisons | reversed comparisons | shuffled shifts " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &r : rows) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.n, r.sorted.comparisons,
                   r.random.comparisons, r.reversed.comparisons, r.random.shifts);
        n.push_back(r.n);
        random.push_back(r.random.comparisons);
        sorted.push_back(r.sorted.comparisons);
        reversed.push_back(r.reversed.comparisons);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(n, random, "one shuffle", {202, 138, 4}, 2).line(n, sorted, "sorted",
                                                            {22, 163, 74}, 2).line(n, reversed, "reversed", {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Actual comparisons: original seed-one workload").x_label("input size").y_label("key comparisons").y_limits(0, 24000).save_svg("build/insertion_profile.svg");
}
```
