\alttext(After sorting one two two, the two equal records retain original indices zero then two; the held later equal key stays after its predecessor.)

> Validation and reference

Native sanitizer checks enumerate all 29524 ternary inputs through length nine
and all 40320 permutations of eight distinct values. Independent stable sorting
of original indices verifies final tie order and every prefix/suffix state;
quadratic pair enumeration verifies inversion and strict-new-minimum counts.
Original states, integer extremes, sorted/reversed formulas, complete caps and
ownership are checked separately. The existing comparison-sort consumers pass.

The reference is
[NIST's insertion sort entry|https://xlinux.nist.gov/dads/HTML/insertionSort.html].
This implementation uses strict predecessor shifts and final placement rather
than an adjacent-swap variant. The examples establish stable ordering and exact
selected work, without claiming universal speed superiority for small arrays or
treating caller-visible input copies as constant storage.

Independent Python prefix-order and pair-count checks verify 1350 inputs, 6784
actual insertion states and all 40 original workload rows. The extracted
original comparison-count function agrees on every retained shuffled input.
Fresh coverage checks pass 42 definitions, 11 compiled public examples and four
clangd hovers.
